  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AT-C 305.35, the examination report on a financial forecast must include a caveat that prospective results may not be achieved because events and circumstances frequently do not occur as expected. AT-C 305.A44 explains this is necessary because actual results will invariably differ from the forecast.
Wrong (A): No forecast can be guaranteed to be achieved. The caveat exists specifically to warn users that actual results will differ from the projected amounts.
